From: Crunch41 <70764418+Crunch41@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:30:05 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Run the room as a container service

The standalone room is written for a desktop console: it waits for
"Q+Enter" on stdin, ignores signals and logs for emulator debugging. In a
container stdin is closed, docker stop sends SIGTERM, and the log is what
docker logs shows.

Stopping:

- The stdin loop is replaced by a once-a-second check of the room state
  and a flag set by SIGINT and SIGTERM. Stopping the process now runs the
  normal shutdown path: ban list save, announce cleanup, room Destroy().
  The ban list is saved before the room unregisters from the lobby,
  which waits on the network: a stop that runs out of time (docker stop
  allows 10 seconds) then can't lose the bans.
- --username takes a required argument. With optional_argument,
  "--username name" left optarg null and crashed when it was read.

Logging:

- Lines carry the local wall-clock time (TZ) instead of the uptime, and
  no source file, line, function or colour codes. Warnings and errors
  keep their class and level:
    [10:28:01] Network <Warning> Dropping malformed LDN packet (3 bytes)
- The console is flushed after every line, so docker logs is current.
- Upstream logs in place on whichever thread logs (room, announce,
  main), with nothing guarding the backends: the file backend's byte
  count and its enabled flag were raced. Writes to the backends are now
  serialised with a mutex. A backend that fails logs the failure (a full
  disk makes the log file's flush log an error), which comes back to the
  backends on the same thread while it holds that mutex: such a nested
  message is dropped instead of deadlocking the logger and hanging the
  room. GetDirectFormatArgs, now used only by the Android backend, is
  marked [[maybe_unused]] so Clang's -Werror builds still pass.

Tests: tests/test_room_protocol.py and the image's startup check stop the
room with SIGTERM and require a clean exit, not a kill, and that a public
room writes its ban list when it stops; a room whose log file can't be
written must still stop cleanly.
